  "articleBody": "Changing the layout of your home with new doorways can transform how your space feels, but certain situations call for skilled structural experience rather than simple hand tools. Here is how to know when to bring in an experienced contractor.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n- The wall is load-bearing: If the wall supports ceiling joists, second-story floors, or roof trusses, you need proper temporary shoring and structural header sizing to avoid settling.\n- Creating an oversized or double-door opening: Wide spans like French doors or pocket doors place extra demand on header integrity and require precise framing tolerances.\n- Hidden mechanicals in the wall cavity: When vents, plumbing stacks, or main electrical runs sit right where your new door belongs, trades must be safely coordinated.\n- Exterior wall modifications: Cutting through exterior sheathing, siding, and weather barriers introduces moisture risks and thermal bridging that need proper detailing.\n- Permitted renovations: Structural wall alterations often involve local building permits and inspections to verify code compliance.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nIf your project involves structural walls or wide spans, having a hands-on general contractor manage the framing keeps your home safe and square. HH Remodeling LLC handles custom framing, drywall repair, and finish carpentry throughout the Denver area. Call Abraham at 303-505-0866 to get started.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
